re made AFTER the requirement states were captured, OR the requirement states reflect what's still ready to be worked on. The instructions say to only propose tasks for R-items with status 'ready', and requirement_states shows the current state. Tasks 4998-5001 committed code but the requirement_states still shows these as 'ready' — meaning they haven't been marked complete yet. But I also need to consider that closed issues represent completed work I shouldn't re-propose. Let me trust requirement_states as the authoritative source since that's what the instructions specify. I've identified 9 remaining ready requirements across three groups, but I need to verify their weights against the constraint that each task can't exceed 4 total weight. Since I can't access the requirements file and can't use tools, I'll assume each requirement has a default weight of 1. Looking at the priority order, the foundational batch 0 release includes four key services, with srd001-testutils being one of them that needs these requirements completed. Looking at the task coverage, I notice task 5000 supposedly handled R3.1-R3.6, but the remaining items still include R3.2, R3.4, R3.5, and R3.6—so either those requirements weren't fully completed or there's overlap I need to clarify by checking the actual contract exports and what each task delivered. The requirement_states data is more reliable than the task title, so R3.2, R3.4, R3.5, and R3.6 still need to be completed. Since I can't access the actual weights in requirements.yaml, I'll work with the assumption that each requirement has a weight of 1 unless the context indicates otherwise, and I need to stay within the constraint of 4 tasks maximum with a total weight of 4 or less. Let me start proposing tasks for the remaining srd001-testutils requirements, then move on to other release 00.0 components like srd002-sys.\n\nI'm counting up the ready requirements: R1.2, R1.3, R1.4, R3.2, R3.4, R3.5, R3.6, R5.1, and R5.2 gives me 9 total. Splitting these across tasks with a 4-requirement maximum means I can group them as Task 0 with R1.2, R1.3, and R1.4, Task 1 with R3.2, R3.4, R3.5, and R3.6, and Task 2 with R5.1 and R5.2. That leaves room for one more task covering a different component.\n\nLooking at the package contracts, I can see what these requirement groups likely represent: R1 covers the core DiffTest struct fields like Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, and ExpectedFiles; R3 handles comparison and normalization features including NormalizeFunc and ComposeNormalizers; and R5 addresses additional functionality like TimestampNormalizer and BuildBinary. The previous tasks have already laid groundwork—Task 4998 created stubs, Task 4999 implemented the core RunDiffTests logic, and Task 5000 handled environment variables, working directories, file expectations, and normalizer composition.\n\nThe remaining work falls into three groups: R1.2-R1.4 likely involves DiffTest struct validation or initialization logic; R3.2, R3.4-R3.6 probably cover specific normalizer behaviors and comparison logic; and R5.1-R5.2 would address test helpers or additional utilities. Since I can't access the SRD directly, I'll structure the next tasks to cover these gaps and reference the SRD in the required reading so the stitch agent can fill in the precise details.\n\nFor srd002-sys, I notice the contract is already defined in package_contracts but no contract task has been created yet—only the testutils contract was set up in task 4998. So I should propose a contract task for that module as well. My plan is four tasks: implement the remaining R1 requirements, handle the R3 group, cover R5, and create the srd002-sys contract stubs.\n\nNow I need to write proper task descriptions with the correct SRD file paths and code locations. For srd001-testutils, the spec is likely at `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd001-testutils.yaml` and the implementation goes in `pkg/testutils/`, probably in `difftest.go` since the main testutils file is forbidden by P7. The contract stubs from the earlier task should already exist. I'll frame these tasks around the requirement IDs and have the stitch agent reference the SRD directly rather than guessing at specifics.\n\nFor srd002-sys, I should propose the contract task first since that package doesn't have one yet, even though all its requirements are marked ready. The contract will define the stubs, then implementation tasks can fill them in. So my four tasks are: testutils R1.2/R1.3/R1.4, testutils R3.2/R3.4/R3.5/R3.6, the sys contract, and then the sys implementation tasks.\n\nI'm assuming weight 1 for each requirement since I can't access the requirements file directly, though I know the weight system exists to prevent oversized tasks—complex requirements can be weight 2-4, so I'm keeping each task to at most 4 requirements to stay safe.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":60706,"cache_read_input_tokens":11311,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":60706},"output_tokens":25,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fec684d9-dd7a-42bc-8a11-11f80fe01182","uuid":"449f775d-5c7f-4af6-b7ac-041c1b323a2f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_015cgfxvhHiPvSBjs8qDm1ic","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Go reimplementations of GNU coreutils/moreutils utilities, verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. The goal is to stress-test a specification-driven AI code generation pipeline.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract, specify, synthesize, verify). Shared libraries in `pkg/` (testutils, sys, format, hashutil, sizeparse, encutil), per-utility implementations in `cmd/`, specifications in `docs/specs/`.\n\n**Current state**: Recent commits (tasks 4998-5001) built out `pkg/testutils` — contract stubs, RunDiffTests core (R2.1-R2.4), Env/WorkDir/ExpectedFiles/ComposeNormalizers/TimestampNormalizer (R2.5-R2.6, R3.1-R3.6 attempted), and BuildBinary (R4.1-R4.4). Requirement states show remaining ready items for srd001-testutils: R1.2, R1.3, R1.4, R3.2, R3.4, R3.5, R3.6, R5.1, R5.2.\n\n**Current release**: rel00.0 (Batch 0 — foundational infrastructure). All seven use cases have codestatus \"not started\" per the analysis, but testutils has partial implementation from recent commits.\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\n1. **Finish srd001-testutils** — 9 remaining ready requirements across 3 groups\n2. **Start srd002-sys** — all 16 requirements ready, needs contract first\n3. Other rel00.0 components (format, hashutil, sizeparse, encutil, magefiles) depend on sys/testutils\n\n## Weight Budget Check\n\nAssuming default weight 1 for all remaining testutils requirements (no evidence of higher weights for these leaf requirements):\n\n- Task 0: R1.2(w=1) + R1.3(w=1) + R1.4(w=1) = 3 — OK\n- Task 1: R3.2(w=1) + R3.4(w=1) + R3.5(w=1) + R3.6(w=1) = 4 — OK\n- Task 2: R5.1(w=1) + R5.2(w=1) = 2 — OK\n- Task 3: srd002-sys contract — no SRD requirements consumed, contract only\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] pkg/testutils: DiffTest validation and error reporting (srd001-testutils R1.2-R1.4)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd001-testutils.yaml (R1.2, R1.3, R1.4 -- the requirements to implement)\n      - pkg/testutils/ (all existing .go files -- understand current implementation state)\n      - CLAUDE.md (project rules and differential testing pattern)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/testutils/difftest.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add R1.2-R1.4 functionality to existing DiffTest infrastructure\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd001-testutils R1.2 -- see SRD for exact specification\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd001-testutils R1.3 -- see SRD for exact specification\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd001-testutils R1.4 -- see SRD for exact specification\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Read the SRD requirements R1.2, R1.3, R1.4 carefully and implement exactly what they specify. Do not invent behavior not in the SRD.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"The pkg/testutils package already has DiffTest, NormalizeFunc, RunDiffTests, ComposeNormalizers, TimestampNormalizer, and BuildBinary implemented. Modify existing files rather than creating new ones.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"The package must not import any cmd/ package or any other pkg/ package per the contract constraints.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"srd001-testutils R1.2 is fully implemented per the SRD specification\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"srd001-testutils R1.3 is fully implemented per the SRD specification\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"srd001-testutils R1.4 is fully implemented per the SRD specification\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"go build ./pkg/testutils/... compiles without errors\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/testutils/... passes without warnings\"\n\n- index: 1\n  title: \"[stitch] pkg/testutils: comparison and normalization features (srd001-testutils R3.2, R3.4-R3.6)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd001-testutils.yaml (R3.2, R3.4, R3.5, R3.6 -- the requirements to implement)\n      - pkg/testutils/ (all existing .go files -- understand current implementation including RunDiffTests, ComposeNormalizers, TimestampNormalizer)\n      - CLAUDE.md (project rules and differential testing pattern)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/testutils/difftest.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add R3.2, R3.4-R3.6 functionality to existing comparison and normalization code\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd001-testutils R3.2 -- see SRD for exact specification\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd001-testutils R3.4 -- see SRD for exact specification\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement srd001-testutils R3.5 -- see SRD for exact specification\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement srd001-testutils R3.6 -- see SRD for exact specification\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Read the SRD requirements R3.2, R3.4, R3.5, R3.6 carefully and implement exactly what they specify. Do not invent behavior not in the SRD.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"RunDiffTests, ComposeNormalizers, and TimestampNormalizer already exist. R3.1 and R3.3 are already complete. Build on the existing normalization and comparison infrastructure.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"The package must not import any cmd/ package or any other pkg/ package per the contract constraints.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"srd001-testutils R3.2 is fully implemented per the SRD specification\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"srd001-testutils R3.4 is fully implemented per the SRD specification\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"srd001-testutils R3.5 is fully implemented per the SRD specification\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"srd001-testutils R3.6 is fully implemented per the SRD specification\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"go build ./pkg/testutils/... compiles without errors\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/testutils/... passes without warnings\"\n\n- index: 2\n  title: \"[stitch] pkg/testutils: test execution helpers (srd001-testutils R5.1-R5.2)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd001-testutils.yaml (R5.1, R5.2 -- the requirements to implement)\n      - pkg/testutils/ (all existing .go files -- understand current implementation state)\n      - CLAUDE.md (project rules and differential testing pattern)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/testutils/difftest.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add R5.1-R5.2 functionality to existing test helpers\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement srd001-testutils R5.1 -- see SRD for exact specification\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement srd001-testutils R5.2 -- see SRD for exact specification\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Read the SRD requirements R5.1, R5.2 carefully and implement exactly what they specify. Do not invent behavior not in the SRD.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"The pkg/testutils package already has DiffTest, RunDiffTests, BuildBinary, ComposeNormalizers, and TimestampNormalizer. Extend the existing code rather than creating new files.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"The package must not import any cmd/ package or any other pkg/ package per the contract constraints.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"srd001-testutils R5.1 is fully implemented per the SRD specification\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"srd001-testutils R5.2 is fully implemented per the SRD specification\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"go build ./pkg/testutils/... compiles without errors\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/testutils/... passes without warnings\"\n\n- index: 3\n  title: \"[stitch] pkg/sys: FileInfo, Stat, Lstat, TerminalWidth, IsTerminal, InstallSIGPIPEHandler, OnTerminalResize contract stubs (srd002-sys)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd002-sys.yaml (full SRD -- understand all exported types and functions)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/sys component -- responsibility and capabilities)\n      - CLAUDE.md (project rules, SIGPIPE handling pattern, build conventions)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/sys/fileinfo.go\n        action: create\n        note: FileInfo struct, Stat and Lstat function stubs\n      - path: pkg/sys/terminal.go\n        action: create\n        note: TerminalWidth, IsTerminal, OnTerminalResize function stubs\n      - path: pkg/sys/sigpipe.go\n        action: create\n        note: InstallSIGPIPEHandler function stub\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Define the FileInfo struct with fields: Mode os.FileMode, Size int64, Nlink uint64, Uid uint32, Gid uint32, Rdev uint64, Dev uint64, Ino uint64, Blocks int64, Blksize int64, ModTime time.Time, AccessTime time.Time, ChangeTime time.Time, Info os.FileInfo\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Define Stat(path string) (*FileInfo, error) and Lstat(path string) (*FileInfo, error) as function stubs that return nil, nil\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Define TerminalWidth() (int, error), IsTerminal(fd uintptr) bool, and OnTerminalResize(callback func(width int)) as function stubs\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Define InstallSIGPIPEHandler() as a function stub\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"This is a contract task. All functions must be compilable stubs (return zero values or nil). Do not implement real logic -- that comes in subsequent tasks.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use build tags or platform-specific files (_darwin.go, _linux.go) only if needed for compilation. Prefer a single file per logical group if stubs compile on all platforms.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"The package may import os, os/signal, syscall, time, and golang.org/x/sys/unix. It must not import any cmd/ package or any other pkg/ package.\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"File names derive from the primary exported type: fileinfo.go for FileInfo/Stat/Lstat, terminal.go for TerminalWidth/IsTerminal/OnTerminalResize, sigpipe.go for InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\"\n      - id: D5\n        text: \"The go.mod already includes golang.org/x/sys. Do not modify go.mod.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"FileInfo struct is defined with all fields matching the contract signature\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Stat and Lstat function signatures match the contract exactly\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"TerminalWidth, IsTerminal, and OnTerminalResize function signatures match the contract exactly\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"InstallSIGPIPEHandler function signature matches the contract exactly\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"go build ./pkg/sys/... compiles without errors\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/sys/... passes without warnings\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":60706,"cache_read_input_tokens":11311,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":60706},"output_tokens":25,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fec684d9-dd7a-42bc-8a11-11f80fe01182","uuid":"afe8d67a-1b52-4154-8cc9-f81782250cc8"}
